@doc """
Settings for a `Request.Parser` or a `Response.Parser`. Every field
has a default, so a call site names only what it changes, as in
`Parser.Options{max_header_bytes: 65536}`.

`max_header_bytes` caps the head, which is the start line and the
headers with the empty line that ends them. It also caps one chunk
size line and the trailers of a chunked body. The default is 16 KiB.

A parser has no limit for a body, because it holds none. The owner
that joins the `Data` events counts the bytes.
"""
struct Parser.Options
  max_header_bytes: Int = 16384
end
